#: ../../source/nanomatch_README.md:115
msgid "What is nanomatch?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nanomatch_README.md:117
msgid ""
"Nanomatch is a fast and accurate glob matcher with full support for "
"standard Bash glob features, including the following \"metacharacters\": "
"`*`, `**`, `?` and `[...]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nanomatch_README.md:119
msgid "**Learn more**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nanomatch_README.md:121
msgid ""
"[Getting started](#getting-started): learn how to install and begin using"
" nanomatch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nanomatch_README.md:122
msgid ""
"[Features](#features): jump to info about supported patterns, and a glob "
"matching reference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nanomatch_README.md:123
msgid "[API documentation](#api): jump to available options and methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nanomatch_README.md:124
msgid ""
"[Unit tests](test): visit unit tests. there is no better way to learn a "
"code library than spending time the unit tests. Nanomatch has 36,000 unit"
" tests - go become a glob matching ninja!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nanomatch_README.md:129
msgid "**Speed and accuracy**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nanomatch_README.md:131
msgid ""
"Nanomatch uses [snapdragon](https://github.com/jonschlinkert/snapdragon) "
"for parsing and compiling globs, which results in:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nanomatch_README.md:133
msgid ""
"Granular control over the entire conversion process in a way that is easy"
" to understand, reason about, and customize."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nanomatch_README.md:134
msgid ""
"Faster matching, from a combination of optimized glob patterns and "
"(optional) caching."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nanomatch_README.md:135
msgid ""
"Much greater accuracy than minimatch. In fact, nanomatch passes _all of "
"the spec tests_ from bash, including some that bash still fails. However,"
" since there is no real specification for globs, if you encounter a "
"pattern that yields unexpected match results [after researching previous "
"issues](../../issues), [please let us know](../../issues/new)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nanomatch_README.md:137
msgid "**Basic globbing only**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nanomatch_README.md:139
msgid ""
"Nanomatch supports [basic globbing only](#features), which is limited to "
"`*`, `**`, `?` and regex-like brackets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nanomatch_README.md:141
msgid ""
"If you need support for the other [bash \"expansion\" types](#bash-"
"expansion-libs) (in addition to the wildcard matching provided by "
"nanomatch), consider using "
"[micromatch](https://github.com/micromatch/micromatch) instead. "
"_(micromatch >=3.0.0  uses the nanomatch parser and compiler for basic "
"glob matching)_"
msgstr ""

